IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa12-logic.l4: small helpers shared by the coa12 modules (the Companies Act 2006, ss 495-539). Not a provision of the Act:
-- the section-label rule cannot apply, so every name here begins `coa12 ` (the part id), which no other part can use.
-- Wanted in the core (NEEDS-CORE.md): three-valued AND and OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN, and the pound conversion of a Penalty.
--
-- The three-valued reading used everywhere in coa12 (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, and NOTHING for "not covered".
--   OR : JUST TRUE if either is JUST TRUE; else NOTHING if either is NOTHING; else JUST FALSE.
--   AND: JUST FALSE if either is JUST FALSE; else NOTHING if either is NOTHING; else JUST TRUE.
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa12 either answer holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE OR b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS NOTHING OR b EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa12 both answers hold` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE OR b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF a EQUALS NOTHING OR b EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- A fact a witness can state, as an answer.
GIVEN fact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa12 the answer for the fact` MEANS
    IF fact THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The most a penalty's fine can be, in pounds, when the statutory maximum and level 3 on the standard scale are stated
-- (the Act does not state them: they are INPUTS). NOTHING for "a fine" with no stated limit, for a level other than 3,
-- and for a penalty with no fine. The fraction of the statutory maximum or of the level is applied (a fraction of 1 is the amount itself).
GIVEN p IS A Penalty
      `the statutory maximum in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`coa12 the largest fine the penalty allows, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST limit THEN
        CONSIDER limit
        WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` f THEN JUST (f TIMES `the statutory maximum in pounds`)
        WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` lv f THEN
            IF lv EQUALS 3
            THEN JUST (f TIMES `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds`)
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` amt THEN JUST amt

-- The opposite answer: JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE swap; NOTHING stays NOTHING (not covered is not covered, whichever way it is put).
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa12 the opposite answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A period counted from a day: the act is in time if it was done on the day or within the number of days after it (both ends in).
-- "Within 14 days after the day" is n = 14; "the period of 28 days beginning with the day" is n = 27, since the day itself is the first.
-- No date (NOTHING) means the act was not done.
GIVEN done IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER done
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN d AT LEAST `the day` AND d AT MOST `the day` PLUS n
